ENGINE core-0201 (applied by engine/guest/base.sh AFTER the product's 0001 0002 0009 0010 libzync/0101): Core's SHA-256
in OpenVM's native state layout. RISC Zero's sys_sha_compress takes the state byte-swapped from Core's uint32_t s[8];
OpenVM's zkvm_sha256_impl takes Core's layout as is. So Transform (0002/0009), HAZYNC_D64_STREAM's hz_d64 (0101) and
HAZYNC_SHA_STREAM's CSHA256 (0101) call zkvm_sha256_impl directly with no swaps; the digest is written big-endian at
the end, as Core's own Finalize does. Same bytes in, same digest out. Made with diff -u in the laid-out tree.

